_np = [['Write down your customer, your offer and your one main channel in three short sentences before spending anything, and revisit them after each month of results.', 'Learn the basic funnel of awareness, interest, action and loyalty, and note one measurable number for each stage so you can see where people drop away.'], ['Interview five real or likely customers for ten minutes each and record the exact words they use, then reuse those phrases in your headlines and posts.', 'Create one short audience profile with age range, main problem, preferred platform and buying trigger, and keep it visible while you plan content.'], ["Write each offer as a benefit plus a deadline or limit, for example 'free setup guide when you order before Friday', and compare two versions of the headline.", 'Keep one clear call to action per message; a post asking people to buy, follow and share all at once usually gets fewer actions than a single request.'], ['Choose a main phrase people would type, put it in the page title, the first heading and the opening paragraph, and keep the title under about 60 characters.', 'Check that your site loads in under three seconds on a phone and that the contact details are visible without scrolling, as slow or hidden pages lose visitors.'], ['Plan a simple content calendar of three posts a week for four weeks, mixing teaching, proof and offers, so you never face a blank page on a busy day.', 'Reuse one idea in several forms, such as a short video, a quote image and a caption thread, and track which form earns the most replies.'], ['Collect email addresses only with a clear tick-box and a plain explanation of what you will send, and keep a record of when and how each person agreed.', 'Include a working unsubscribe link and your business details in every email, and remove anyone who opts out within a few days rather than weeks.'], ['Set up a simple tracking sheet with date, channel, spend, visits and sales, and review it every Friday for fifteen minutes to spot what to repeat or stop.', "Compare each channel's cost per sale rather than total visits, because a channel with fewer visitors can still bring the cheapest customers."], ['At the end of each month, keep one thing that worked, fix one thing that nearly worked, and stop one thing that did not, then write the plan for next month.', 'Present your results to a friend in five minutes using three numbers and one lesson, which checks whether you truly understand your own marketing.']]
C['mods'] = [(m[0], m[1], list(m[2])+_np[i], m[3], m[4], m[5]) for i, m in enumerate(C['mods'])]

